From: Enceka <enceka@yeah.net>
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: bypass short IPv4 before CT WLAN offload

CT WED cannot transmit Ethernet frames shorter than 72 bytes through the
hardware egress path. This includes TCP acknowledgements and control
packets. Classify untagged IPv4 packets with total length 20..57 at the
wired ingress and send them to CPU RX ring 1 before PPE forwarding.

Acquire an unused IFC classifier, scope it to the GDM4 Ethernet ingress,
and admit WLAN flow offload only when that ingress is covered. Preserve
port configuration changes while scoped, verify programmed state, and
restore owned state after draining PPE; failed restoration remains
retryable. If the classifier is unavailable, retain software WLAN egress.

